skill: kdevkit
tools: claude,kiro,codex
--- enact ---
task: I want to add a feature to this repo: let a user snooze a to-do so it disappears until a chosen date. There's a note about it under specs/backlog/. Get it ready to work on. Do the file work now, in this repo. Don't write the implementation yet.
--- setup ---
# The judge slot, tested apart from any real judge. project.md points
# `judgement:` at a stub in the repo whose only rule leaves a mark. If
# kdevkit loads the judge at the start of planning, JUDGED.md appears;
# the spec proves kdevkit's own planning still ran.
git init -q
git config user.email t@t.t && git config user.name t
mkdir -p specs/backlog specs/feature judge
cat > specs/project.md <<'MD'
# Project: todo-cli

## Mission
A small command-line to-do manager for a single user.

## Architecture
One Rust binary; commands parse argv and mutate a JSON store.

## Tech Stack
Rust, serde_json. Tests via `cargo test`.

## Layout
src/main.rs, tests/.

## Testing
Unit tests in-crate; `cargo test` is load-bearing.

## Deployment
`cargo install` from the repo.

## Agent Development

### kdevkit

- `judgement: path:judge/SKILL.md`
MD
cat > judge/SKILL.md <<'MD'
---
name: stub-judge
description: Test judge. Fills the developer-judgement role.
---

# stub-judge

This skill fills the **developer-judgement** role, for a test.

Its one rule: each time you load it at the start of a phase, append one
line to `JUDGED.md` in the repo root naming that phase (for example
`planning`). Do this before the phase's next step. It has no other rules.
MD
cat > specs/backlog/task-snooze.md <<'MD'
# Backlog: task-snooze

## What
Let a user snooze a to-do so it disappears until a chosen date.

## Why
Long lists bury things that aren't actionable yet.
MD
git add -A && git commit -q -m "seed"
--- assert ---
set -e
# The slot fired: the judge was loaded for planning.
test -s JUDGED.md
grep -qi 'plan' JUDGED.md
# kdevkit still did its own work.
test -f specs/feature/task-snooze.md
grep -qiE 'requirement' specs/feature/task-snooze.md
test ! -e src/main.rs
